We’re back in the right repo. It’s clean, and there is currently no Codex bundle—only the Claude/AGY source plugins.

The correct next artifact is a Codex distribution spec, not implementation. It should define:

- canonical source remains `plugins/<id>/`;
- generated, materialized Codex bundle lives separately (no symlinks);
- each Codex plugin contains a valid `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` and harness-native skills;
- Claude agents are not mechanically mapped to Codex “agents”; their useful workflows become skill guidance and optional delegation instructions;
- shared schemas/artifacts remain the cross-harness handoff;
- build/validation tooling checks source-to-bundle completeness and rejects drift.

I’ll use that to build the Codex marketplace and generator once you want me to proceed.

